# 30. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

Implement the following critical rules:

1. Every product must belong to a pharmaceutical company.
2. Each product may have multiple batches.
3. Each batch must have a manufacturing date and expiry date where applicable.
4. The same product can exist in multiple warehouses.
5. Sales must automatically reduce stock.
6. Purchases must automatically increase stock after GRN confirmation.
7. Purchase returns must reduce stock.
8. Sales returns must increase saleable stock only after inspection and approval.
9. Expired products must never be available for normal sale.
10. FEFO must be the default batch selection policy.
11. Every sales invoice must update customer accounts.
12. Every purchase invoice must update company payable accounts.
13. Every payment must update the relevant financial ledger.
14. Every approved return must update the relevant stock and financial accounts.
15. Every financial transaction must have a unique reference.
16. Deleted or cancelled transactions must retain their audit history.
17. Every stock adjustment must require authorization.
18. Every discount beyond configured limits must require approval.
19. Every company must have separate financial reporting.
20. Consolidated reports must combine all company records without mixing their identities.
21. Every stock movement must have a traceable source transaction.
22. No financial record should be permanently deleted through normal application operations.
23. Opening balances must be configurable during initial setup.
24. Reports must reflect actual posted transactions, not merely draft documents.

